From 1740637f297ea2637dd7d936d5a96977d5cc2343 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: atomozero <bernardi.andrea@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 14:19:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 011/203] ehci: support device tree controllers with an
 integrated TT (Tegra 2)

- Split the PCI specific parts (AMD workaround, BAR mapping, BIOS
  handoff, MSI) from the controller setup in the constructor, and add a
  constructor for controllers that are not on a PCI bus.
- Add an attachment for enabled 'nvidia,tegra20-ehci' device tree nodes,
  whose EHCI registers start at offset 0x100. The UTMI/ULPI PHYs are
  expected to have been set up by the boot firmware for now.
- Add kIntegratedTT for ChipIdea/TDI cores, which have no companion
  controllers: full and low speed devices (keyboards, mice) are not handed
  off, the port speed is read from PORTSC, and the controller is put back
  into host mode (USBMODE) after a reset.

The PCI path was tested with QEMU's usb-ehci and a USB storage device;
the device tree and integrated TT paths are not tested on hardware yet.
